  "inputHtml": "<html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<title>Quadratic formula - Encyclopedia</title>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"content\">\n<h1>Quadratic Formula</h1>\n<div class=\"mw-parser-output\">\n\n<p>In algebra, the <b>quadratic formula</b> gives the solutions of the general quadratic equation. Given a second-degree polynomial of the form <span class=\"mwe-math-element\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"ax^{2}+bx+c=0\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ax^{2}+bx+c=0</annotation></semantics></math></span><img class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline\" src=\"https://example.com/math/quad.svg\" alt=\"ax^{2}+bx+c=0\"></span>, the values of <i>x</i> satisfying this equation are given by the quadratic formula.</p>\n\n<p>The formula is expressed as:</p>\n\n<dl><dd><span class=\"mwe-math-element\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x={\\frac {-b\\pm {\\sqrt {b^{2}-4ac}}}{2a}}\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#xB1;</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x={\\frac {-b\\pm {\\sqrt {b^{2}-4ac}}}{2a}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-display\" src=\"https://example.com/math/quadformula.svg\" alt=\"x={\\frac {-b\\pm {\\sqrt {b^{2}-4ac}}}{2a}}\"></span></dd></dl>\n\n<p>The quantity under the square root, <span class=\"mwe-math-element\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b^{2}-4ac\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{2}-4ac</annotation></semantics></math></span><img class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline\" src=\"https://example.com/math/disc.svg\" alt=\"b^{2}-4ac\"></span>, is known as the <b>discriminant</b>. Its value determines the nature of the solutions.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
